      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it may handy to keep sendDtmfString(string, on, off, local)\nbut there may not be a piratical way to guarantee the on/off period.\nSo please document this API clearly so that developers know the on/off time is not guaranteed but as best effort.\n\nHere are the reasons,\n\nWhen calling sendDtmf(), you just put the DTMF_START request into the queue. The RIL may or may not get it right way. Similar happens to stopDtmf(). So the sleep(dtmfOn) between sendDtmf and stopDtmf defines the period between putting DTMF requests in QUEUE rather than the period of start and stop the tone. That is why I said \"the tone length can be either shorten or lengthen than API specified\".",
      "revId": "d3215eab58362b0d7dbe8351e2b6392b34bb95aa",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
